# Repositories and projects

- `internal/git` (clone, pull, branch via the host `git` binary) is legacy code kept compiling but **not wired to any HTTP route**; task B hardens it and implements the planned `/api/v1/projects` routes (types in `internal/apitypes/projects.go`, table `projects`, store methods in `internal/store/projects.go`).
- Checkouts belong under the data directory's `repositories/` (`datadir.Layout.Repositories()`), never relative to the working directory. Validate names and derived paths before filesystem or command operations.
- Clone, pull and branch switches run as jobs (`project.clone`, `project.pull`, `project.branch`) with subject `("project", id)`; update the project's transient status (`cloning`, `pulling`, `switching_branch`) and restore a terminal one on every exit path.
- Credentials are stored encrypted in `projects.auth_secret` (purpose `secrets.ProjectAuthPurpose(id)`) and never returned, logged or written to job logs; responses expose only `auth_type`, `auth_username` and `has_secret`.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/git/... ./internal/store/...`.
